# TODO - Boundary and dependency contracts

## Objective

Protect ownership and dependency direction across authored source.

## Acceptance

- Require meaningful Boundary-Contract headers on authored code.
- Test workspace inheritance and prevent member-level lint weakening.
- Reject shared-to-title, shared-to-tool and title-to-title dependencies.
- Separate source-media adapters from runtime and platform adapters.

## Evidence

Fresh `cargo validate --no-cache` passed on Linux x86-64 on 2026-11-24.
The validator now checks authored code for ownership headers and rejects
member-level lint overrides or uninherited dependencies. Dependency direction
checks reject shared-to-title, shared-to-tool, title-to-title and prohibited
runtime/importer/platform edges. Synthetic negative controls cover missing
headers, malformed ownership fields, lint weakening, undeclared dependencies
and forbidden dependency directions. No original game media was required.

These checks protect crate-level dependency boundaries. Fine-grained
capability reuse and clone detection remain separate pending contracts.
